  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between 3-Methylenenorvaline and the serine/threonine-protein kinase CDC2L1, as this compound is implicated in multiple pathways targeting different entities. Path_40292 and Path_40293 both indicate that 3-Methylenenorvaline acts as a target of SW-60, which in turn is a target of CDC2L1. This implies that 3-Methylenenorvaline may interact with SW-60, which is a known target of CDC2L1, suggesting a possible mechanism of action involving the modulation of CDC2L1 activity. Path_40294 further supports this by showing that 3-Methylenenorvaline targets a sodium/bile acid cotransporter, which is also a target of CDC2L1. This indicates that 3-Methylenenorvaline may influence multiple pathways that ultimately affect CDC2L1. The integration of these pathways highlights the compound's potential to modulate CDC2L1 through diverse mechanisms, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
